@startuml
!include style/ail.puml
title G7 · Callback timelines: when the API has finished using the handler
hide footbox
$caller(client, "Program\nRegisters and ends callback use")
$callee(api, "Library API\nInvokes the handler")
$callee(handler, "Handler\nRuns the callback")
== Constructed call-scoped operation ==
note over client, handler
  Program enters registration.
  API borrows the handler for this call.
end note
api -[dotted]> handler : API starts the handler during registration
activate handler
note over handler : Handler finishes.
deactivate handler
note over client, handler
  Registration completes. Every handler invocation has finished.
  This registration can start no more. API retains no handler.
end note
note over api, handler
  count(1, 1): if this call eventually completes,
  it has invoked the handler once.
  scope(call) bounds use to this call.
  quiescence(return) ends all use at completion.
end note
== Synthetic owner-scoped subscription: successful registration ==
note over client, handler
  Program enters subscribe. API borrows the handler
  and keeps its own strong reference for the returned subscription.
end note
api -> client : subscribe returns: give the program\na Subscription to destroy
note over api, handler
  After subscribe returns, API may start the handler:
  timing(after_return).
end note
api -[dotted]> handler : API starts one permitted notification
activate handler
note over client, handler
  Program begins unsubscribe from outside this callback.
  The handler can still be running on another thread.
end note
client -> api : At unsubscribe entry: transfer\nresponsibility for Subscription
note over handler : The running handler finishes\nduring teardown.
deactivate handler
note over client, handler
  unsubscribe returns. Every handler invocation has finished.
  This subscription can start no more: quiescence(@unsubscribe).
end note
note over api, handler
  scope(owner($result)) ties use to the subscription's lifetime.
  count(0, many) permits zero or more notifications.
  This trace shows one.
end note
legend bottom
  Time runs downward within separate cases; spacing is not duration.
  Actor = program; rectangles = callees (API calls Handler in each dotted arrow).
  Bars = active handler invocations; dotted arrow = callback entry; solid arrow = ownership transfer.
  Notes mark completion; no arrow denotes an ordinary return. Non-normative: C3, C6, F1.
  outside_callback keeps unsubscribe outside the callback it waits for.
  Neither case promises that the enclosing operation will eventually finish.
  Native scheduling and capture-release machinery are omitted.
endlegend
@enduml
